<<~ ahu slot=`#/browser-vm-global-detection-hand-back`>>

! Browser VM global detection hand-back

Changed `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-host-bridge.ts` to snapshot enumerable host-global keys at each sandboxed module invocation and filter TW5's global-check epilogue against that snapshot. A stack preserves the outer snapshot during nested module invocations. Added `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/browser-vm-shim-globals.test.ts` using the real browser-worker genesis boot. Updated the existing browser-worker control in `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/genesis-boot.test.ts` to add its global during module execution.

Before the fix, `npx vitest run tests/browser-vm-shim-globals.test.ts` ran both tests and both failed: the clean module reported existing globals, and the leak reported those globals plus `leakedByModule`.

After the fix, the same command stopped at <code>[vitest-dist-guard] &#64;lararium/tw5 stale build</code>; no green result was obtained. The seat law requires stopping at this guard and assigns the build to the lead. The requested build and the new, browser-host-bridge, and genesis-boot tests remain for the lead. No e2e ran. `pnpm exec tsc -p tsconfig.typecheck.json --noEmit` passed; a subsequent small edit restricted replacement to the check epilogue. No commit or git write occurred.

<<~/ahu>>

